  "question": {
    "text": "If two distinct numbers&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></math> are selected from the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><msup><mn>5</mn><mn>9</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>,&nbsp;then the probability that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>log</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></math> is an integer is",
